SEG = "FLD"
CAT = "fqField"
Q = [
    ("Principle 3 of the National Firearms Safety Code says to ensure your firing zone is clear and to identify your target:",
     "Beyond all doubt", ["Within 100 metres", "Through your scope", "By its colour"],
     "Principle 3 says always ensure your firing zone is clear and identify your target beyond all doubt. If in doubt, do not shoot."),
    ("You see bushes move and hear rustling where you expect a pig. The Code says to:",
     "Wait until it is identified", ["Fire low into the movement", "Fire one warning shot", "Fire where the sound came from"],
     "The Code says do not fire at movement, colour, sound or shape only. You must be certain that what you see is your target."),
    ("Early in the morning or late in the evening, the Code says you should shoot only when the target is:",
     "Identified and in full view", ["Moving away from you", "Within your scope's view", "Lit by the vehicle's headlights"],
     "The Code says it is hard to see clearly at those times, so the object must be clearly identified and in full view before you shoot."),
    ("Under the National Firearms Safety Code, your firing zone includes:",
     "The area beyond the target", ["Only the area to the target", "Only the area you can see", "Only the area within 50 m"],
     "The Code says the firing zone is not only the area between you and the target but also the area beyond it that is still within the extreme range of your firearm."),
    ("The National Firearms Safety Code gives the effective danger range of a .22 rimfire as about:",
     "1.5 km", ["150 m", "500 m", "4.0 km"],
     "The Code lists about 1,500 metres for .22 rimfire, 3.6 km for .303, about 4 km for .308 and 150 metres for an air rifle."),
    ("The National Firearms Safety Code gives the effective danger range of an air rifle as about:",
     "150 m", ["15 m", "50 m", "1.5 km"],
     "The Code lists about 150 metres for an air rifle, compared with about 1,500 metres for a .22 rimfire. Air rifles are not toys."),
    ("The National Firearms Safety Code gives the effective danger range of a .308 as about:",
     "4 km", ["1.5 km", "400 m", "10 km"],
     "The Code lists 4,050 metres, about 4 km, for the .308, and 3,600 metres for the .303. A rifle bullet can travel far beyond any target."),
    ("The National Firearms Safety Code gives the danger range of a shotgun firing #6 shot as about:",
     "250 m", ["25 m", "450 m", "1.5 km"],
     "The Code lists about 250 metres for #6 shot and about 450 metres for BB shot."),
    ("Why does a shotgun's firing zone grow at longer distances?",
     "The pellets spread further", ["The pellets speed up", "The recoil is stronger", "The barrel heats up quickly"],
     "The Code explains that shotgun pellets spread further over long distances, so the firing zone increases. Moving targets widen the danger area too."),
    ("According to the Code, shooting at a moving target:",
     "Increases the danger area", ["Shrinks the firing zone", "Removes the ricochet risk", "Needs no backstop at all"],
     "The Code says that when shooting at moving targets the danger area increases, because the target, and so the line of fire, is moving."),
    ("Why does the Code stress correctly aligned sights, especially a telescopic sight?",
     "A miss may hit something else", ["It makes recoil much softer", "It keeps the barrel clean", "It is needed for a licence"],
     "The Code says misaligned sights may make you miss and increase the chance of hitting something you did not intend to hit."),
    ("The National Firearms Safety Code says never to fire at:",
     "Water or hard flat surfaces", ["Targets on a backstop", "Game in open ground", "Paper targets at a club range"],
     "The Code says a ricochet will almost certainly result from shooting at water, smooth flat surfaces or rocks, and you lose control of where the projectile ends up."),
    ("Why does the Code say air rifles are very prone to ricochet?",
     "Their projectiles are slow", ["Their pellets are steel", "Their range is very long", "Their barrels are short"],
     "The Code warns that air rifles should be treated with the utmost caution because the slow velocity of the projectile makes them very prone to ricochet."),
    ("When shooting a shotgun over hard ground or water, the Code says the chance of a ricochet is multiplied by:",
     "The number of pellets", ["The length of the barrel", "The choke size", "The shooter's height"],
     "The Code says a shotgun's ricochet chance is multiplied by the number of pellets in the cartridge, and only one pellet can cause serious injury or death."),
    ("In the field, the Code says a firearm should be carried unloaded with the action open until:",
     "You are in your shooting area", ["You leave the vehicle", "You pass the first gate", "You feel ready to walk"],
     "The Code says firearms should be carried unloaded with the action open until you are in your shooting area and expecting game to be flushed."),
    ("When hunting with others walking line abreast, the Code says to shoot only:",
     "At targets in front of you", ["At any target you see", "At targets behind the line", "When the person beside you fires"],
     "The Code says take a shot only if the target is in front of you, or if you are at the end of the line and can turn away from your companions safely."),
    ("When stalking game with companions walking one behind the other, the Code says the only loaded firearm should be:",
     "The lead person's", ["The last person's", "Everyone's", "The most experienced shooter's"],
     "The Code says that when walking in single file, only the person in the lead should have a loaded firearm."),
    ("When shooting from a boat or punt, the Code says to:",
     "Keep both hands on it", ["Rest it on the gunwale", "Keep it loaded at all times", "Stand up for every shot"],
     "The Code says keep both hands on your firearm and control the muzzle at all times in a boat or punt, and do not carry it loaded unless ready to shoot."),
    ("A cartridge makes an unusual soft sound when fired. Before firing again, the Code says to:",
     "Unload and check the barrel", ["Fire again straight away", "Fire at a softer target", "Clean the scope lens first"],
     "A soft sound can mean the projectile is stuck in the barrel. The Code says check for an obstruction before firing again, and always unload first."),
    ("The Code says barrel obstructions in the field are commonly caused by:",
     "Mud or twigs", ["Light gun oil", "Damp cartridges", "Hot weather"],
     "The Code says barrel obstructions are very common in the field from objects such as mud and twigs lodging in the barrel, so check the barrel often, after unloading."),
    ("Why does the Code say set triggers and hair triggers do not belong in the field?",
     "A knock could set them off", ["They are banned outright", "They spoil accuracy", "They need special ammunition"],
     "The Code says set and hair triggers are designed for target shooting, and in the field a simple knock may cause an unintentional discharge."),
    ("Crossing a fence alone with a firearm, the Code says to unload it, then:",
     "Lay it through and cross away", ["Climb with it slung on your back", "Climb holding it by the barrel", "Hand it over the top as you climb"],
     "The Code says unload, place the firearm through the fence on the ground with the muzzle in a safe direction, and cross the fence away from it."),
    ("Crossing a fence with a friend, one safe method in the Code is to:",
     "Hand them your unloaded gun", ["Both climb with loaded guns", "Hand them your loaded gun", "Climb first, then pull it over"],
     "The Code says make sure all firearms are unloaded, then either lay them through the fence or hand yours to your companion, cross, and have it handed back."),
    ("When looking through a telescopic sight, the Code warns that you may not see objects:",
     "Just beyond the muzzle", ["At the target itself", "Directly behind you", "Far past the target area"],
     "The Code says there is an area at the muzzle and a short distance beyond it that is not visible through a telescopic sight, so check this danger zone before firing."),
    ("The National Firearms Safety Code suggests starting to sight in a rifle from a firing point of:",
     "25 m", ["10 m", "50 m", "200 m"],
     "The Code says the firing point should be set at 25 metres first, then the sights adjusted again firing at a target from 100 metres."),
    ("When zeroing a rifle, the Code says to use a safe backstop such as:",
     "A soft earthen bank", ["A corrugated iron wall", "A large rock face", "A dam's water surface"],
     "The Code recommends a safe backstop such as a soft earthen bank to stop all projectiles. Rock, steel and water cause ricochets."),
    ("When spotlighting at night, the Code reminds you that the only area you can see is:",
     "Inside the spotlight beam", ["Up to the horizon", "Wherever the moon shines", "Within your scope's full range"],
     "The Code says that when using a spotlight the only area you can see is within the beam, so be sure of your target and do not take a doubtful shot."),
    ("Before spotlighting on a host's property, the Code suggests offering to:",
     "Tell neighbouring properties", ["Pay the host's neighbours", "Shoot near the boundary", "Turn off all the vehicle lights"],
     "The Code notes that spotlighting at night can stress owners of adjoining properties, and suggests offering to inform neighbouring properties of your plans."),
]
